config MTK_RAM_CONSOLE
	bool "MediaTek RAM console (last-kmsg via pstore/ramoops)"
	depends on PSTORE_RAM
	depends on MTK_AEE_IPANIC
	default n
	help
	  Enables the MediaTek RAM console driver for the Dimensity 7030
	  (MT6879) platform. The driver:
	
	    * Exposes the previous boot kernel console as /proc/last_kmsg
	      so Android init and bugreport tools can retrieve it early.
	
	    * Reads the bootloader "ram_console" property from /chosen
	      (if present) and appends that SRAM/DRAM log region.
	
	  The persistent write path is provided by aee_sram_printk() from
	  the MTK AEE/mrdump subsystem (CONFIG_MTK_AEE_IPANIC), while
	  CONFIG_PSTORE_RAM plus the ramoops node keeps cross-reboot logs.
	
	  Say Y here to enable debugging of custom-kernel boot failures.
	  If unsure, say N.
